---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content'

const lainey = await getEntry('authors', 'lainey')
const avatarSrc = lainey!.data.avatar
---

<BaseLayout>
	<main class="app-container pt-24">
		<h1 class="text-6xl pb-2 font-bold">About</h1>
	</main>
	<section class="app-container py-12 mb-8">
		<div class="bubble-wrapper">
			<div class="pixel-bubble">
				<div
					class="prose prose-neutral prose-lg md:prose-xl dark:prose-invert prose-img:rounded-xl prose-figure:text-center prose-img:mx-auto"
				>
					<p>
						Research can be intense and often isolating. Most of what we write as postgrads is high stakes: thesis chapters, journal articles, funding applications. These matter, but they are tied to formal outcomes. When writing only "counts" if it is assessed, it becomes easy to associate it with pressure rather than with thinking. Not all writing needs to carry that weight. Writing that supports learning and idea development without evaluation can be just as valuable (<a href="https://www.bard.edu/wwwmedia/files/6790042/3/Elbow%20High%20Stakes%20and%20Low%20Stakes%20Assigning%20and%20Responding.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Elbow, 1997</a>).
					</p>
					<p>
						Writing is an act of thinking, not a way of reporting what you already know. People who write regularly tend to do better academically (<a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.3102/00346543074001029" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bangert-Drowns et al., 2004</a>), and in doctoral writing groups, students learn as much from reading and critiquing each other's work as from receiving feedback on their own (<a href="https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/03075070902785580" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Aitchison, 2009</a>). Writing becomes something you do with people, not something you do alone.
					</p>
					<p>
						That sense of community matters. Postgrads who write together feel more like they belong in their research community (<a href="https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/0307507032000058109" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lee and Boud, 2003</a>), and given that postgraduate researchers report significantly higher levels of anxiety and depression than the general population (<a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/nbt.4089" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Evans et al., 2018</a>), that matters. A blog won't fix structural problems in academia, but it can offer a space to think out loud with people who are going through the same thing.
					</p>
					<p>
						The Ensemble Edit is a student-led space for low-pressure writing across disciplines. You might write about a seminar, a method you're trying, a conference, or just what postgrad life is actually like. Everything is reviewed before it goes on the site, but nothing is formally assessed. The site runs on GitHub, so contributors pick up experience with shared workflows and version control along the way. We want to bring together writers from AIMSIR, Decarb-AI, Co-Centre for Climate + Biodiversity + Water, the School of Maths, and anyone else who is interested.
					</p>
					<p>
						Good research culture comes from people engaging with each other's thinking, beyond formal publications. This blog is one small attempt at that.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<img
				src={avatarSrc}
				alt={lainey!.data.name}
				class="bubble-avatar pixel-hop"
				style="image-rendering: pixelated;"
			/>
		</div>
		<div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-foreground/10 dark:border-foreground-dark/10">
			<p class="text-lg">Interested in writing?</p>
			<a href="/submit/" class="btn-pixel btn-pixel-red btn-pixel-sm mt-4">Contribute</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	/* Wrapper: relative positioning context for bubble + avatar */
	.bubble-wrapper {
		position: relative;
		max-width: min(80ch, 100%);
		/* Space below for avatar overhang */
		margin-bottom: 7rem;
	}

	.bubble-wrapper:hover {
		animation: pixel-wiggle 0.3s steps(2);
	}

	/* Speech bubble — chunky border + triangle tail; responsive by construction */
	.pixel-bubble {
		--pb-border: var(--color-foreground, #000);
		--pb-page: var(--color-background, #ffffff);
		position: relative;
		max-width: 100%;
		border: 4px solid var(--pb-border);
		background: var(--pb-page);
		padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
	}

	.pixel-bubble :global(.prose) {
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}

	:global(.dark) .pixel-bubble {
		--pb-border: var(--color-foreground-dark, #fff);
		--pb-page: #ffffff;
		background-color: #fff;
		color: #000;
	}

	:global(.dark) .pixel-bubble :global(.prose) {
		--tw-prose-body: #000;
		--tw-prose-headings: #000;
		--tw-prose-links: #1a56db;
	}

	/* Tail: down-pointing triangle near the right (outer = border, inner = fill) */
	.pixel-bubble::after {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		bottom: -18px;
		right: 2.5rem;
		width: 0;
		height: 0;
		border-left: 12px solid transparent;
		border-right: 12px solid transparent;
		border-top: 18px solid var(--pb-border);
	}
	.pixel-bubble::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		bottom: -11px;
		right: calc(2.5rem + 4px);
		width: 0;
		height: 0;
		border-left: 8px solid transparent;
		border-right: 8px solid transparent;
		border-top: 12px solid var(--pb-page);
		z-index: 1;
	}

	/* Avatar: below the bubble, kept inside the right edge */
	.bubble-avatar {
		position: absolute;
		bottom: -5rem;
		right: 0;
		height: 5rem;
		width: auto;
		object-fit: contain;
	}

	@media (min-width: 768px) {
		.bubble-avatar {
			bottom: -6rem;
			height: 6rem;
		}
		.pixel-bubble::after {
			right: 3.5rem;
		}
		.pixel-bubble::before {
			right: calc(3.5rem + 4px);
		}
	}
</style>
